    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (source for the generated `OwnerDto`) \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `checkDigit` schema fields with a single `memberId`; updated `fiscalYear` and `locality` descriptions to reference the memberId.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 renamed field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`, with matching getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` (widened to `VARCHAR(32)` since the unified id is longer). The hsqldb schema is what the test suite (ddl-auto=none) actually uses.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `buildCustomerCode` \u2192 `buildMemberId`, now composing `REGION + 2-digit FY + HASH8 + Luhn CHK` (CHK computed over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` via a new `luhnCheckDigit` helper); collision de-dup now runs against existing `memberId` values. Updated the audit log line to emit `memberId` (dropped `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`).\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 removed `toMembershipNumber` and `toCheckDigit` (and their `@Mapping`s); `toFiscalYear` now derives `FY<YY>` from the FY segment inside the memberId; `toLocality` parses `REGION` from the memberId (stripping any `-<n>` collision suffix), falling back to `toRegion`. `memberId` maps implicitly by name.\n\n6. **`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 the audit record's primary-identifier field is now `memberId`.\n\n**Result:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` passes (verified region prefix `NSW`, the SHA-256 HASH8, and absence of the old fields), and the full suite builds green. The audit output confirms the new shape, e.g. `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
